    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Babur established the Mughal Empire after defeating Ibrahim Lodi in the First Battle of Panipat in 1526.",
        "Humayun lost the empire briefly to Sher Shah Suri after the battles of Chausa (1539) and Kannauj (1540), but restored Mughal rule in 1555.",
        "Akbar expanded the empire, introduced the Mansabdari administrative system, abolished Jizya, and initiated the syncretic religion Din-i-Ilahi.",
        "Shah Jahan's reign is widely regarded as the golden age of Mughal architecture, highlighted by the Taj Mahal, Jama Masjid, and Red Fort.",
        "Aurangzeb expanded the empire to its maximum territorial extent but his prolonged Deccan campaign and orthodox policies weakened the imperial authority."
      ],
